course: dictionary
lesson: 9526
title: Words that mean without
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word stingless is made of two parts: sting and -less. The ending -less means without, so stingless means without a sting. «Stingless bees live in warm countries like Brazil, Mexico and Australia.»
explain: The dictionary says stingless means having no sting or no working sting. The example sentence adds a clue: «their stingers are tiny and useless, so they defend by biting and crowding intruders.» A bee that cannot sting still protects its nest, but in a different way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Stingless bees live in warm countries» still makes sense if you think of bees with no working sting. If your meaning fits every time, you are probably right.
fact: Stingless means having no sting or no working sting.
fact: The ending -less means without, so you can work out words like hopeless and careless.
fact: Stingless bees are small bees found in warm countries such as Australia, Brazil and Mexico.
fact: Stingless bees cannot sting, but they protect their nests by biting and crowding intruders.
fact: In Australia, stingless bees are called native bees or sugarbag bees, and they help pollinate crops like macadamia nuts.
exercise: «Stingless bees live in warm countries like Brazil, Mexico and Australia.» What does stingless mean? | Living only in cold places | *Having no sting or no working sting | Having a very long sting | Very loud and buzzy
exercise: «Stingless bees cannot sting, so how do they defend their nests?» | By stinging very hard | By hiding under the sea | *By biting and crowding intruders | By flying away and never coming back
exercise: In the word stingless, what does the ending -less mean? | Very big | Under | Again | *Without
test: «Their stingers are tiny and useless.» What does useless mean here? | *Not working or not able to do the job | Very shiny and bright | Sweet to taste | Heavy and strong
test: Stingless bees are found in warm countries such as Australia, Brazil and Mexico. Which of these is a warm country where they live? | Iceland | Norway | Finland | *Brazil
exam: Which sentence best explains stingless bees? | Stingless bees never make any honey | Stingless bees have huge stings and attack in large swarms | *Stingless bees have tiny useless stingers, so they defend by biting and crowding | Stingless bees fly only in cold countries
